"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia defensive coordinator Glenn Schumann agrees to coach Florida State","description":"Georgia's Glenn Schumann, one of the country's top defensive coordinators and part of a staff that has the Bulldogs at No. 1 in the CFP rankings, agreed to a five-year deal to become the next coach at Florida State, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T00:49:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577665/uga-defensive-coordinator-schumann-coach-florida-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aiden Flora, nation's leading rusher, re-signs with Iowa State for next season","description":"Iowa State running back Aiden Flora, who leads the nation in rushing, announced Monday that he has re-signed with the Cyclones for next season.","published":"2026-11-23T23:57:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577520/aiden-flora-nation-leading-rusher-re-signs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas A&M names John Thornton interim athletic director effective Dec. 1","description":"John Thornton will take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU's Lane Kiffin apologizes for using profanity during halftime interview","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin has apologized for using profanity during a halftime interview with the school's radio network in Saturday's loss to Tennessee.","published":"2026-11-23T20:12:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575735/lsu-kiffin-apologizes-use-profanity-interview","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest leading rusher Ty Clark ruled out for season","description":"Wake Forest running back Ty Clark will miss the rest of the season, coach Jake Dickert announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T20:30:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575731/wake-forest-leading-rusher-ry-clark-ruled-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse rules QB Steve Angeli (shoulder) out vs. Notre Dame","description":"Syracuse has ruled starting quarterback Steve Angeli out for Saturday's game against Notre Dame due to a shoulder injury.","published":"2026-11-23T18:40:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575118/syracuse-rules-qb-steve-angeli-shoulder-vs-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana not yet naming starting QB for game vs. Purdue, Curt Cignetti says","description":"Indiana is not yet naming a starting quarterback for Saturday's rivalry game against Purdue, coach Curt Cignetti said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T18:51:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575086/indiana-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4875127/lanorris-sellers","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LaNorris_Sellers"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"LaNorris Sellers","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LaNorris_Sellers","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:15Z","intro":"LaNorris Sellers (born June 23, 2005) is an American college football quarterback for the South Carolina Gamecocks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sellers was born and raised in Florence, South Carolina. He attended South Florence High School in Florence for all four years of his high school career. As a senior Sellers took the Bruins to the South Carolina 4A State Championship where they beat the Northwestern Trojans 57–30.\nSellers was named the Florence Morning News Prep Football Player of the Year after he passed for 2,948 yards with 45 touchdowns and rushed for 1,338 yards and 17 touchdowns. Sellers was named the offensive MVP of the 2022 Shrine Bowl after throwing for 121 yards and a touchdown.\nAt the conclusion of his high school career Sellers was ranked No. 4 prospect in the state, the 16th-best quarterback in the country and No. 246 overall in the 247Sports Composite. He originally committed to play college football at Virginia and then Syracuse before finally signing with South Carolina."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Sellers began his true freshman season as the backup quarterback to Spencer Rattler. In Week 2 against Furman, he made his collegiate debut, completing all four of his passes for 86 yards and two touchdowns in the victory. In Week 10 against Vanderbilt, he recorded a 36-yard rushing touchdown on his only attempt in the victory. On the season, Sellers appeared in three games while preserving his redshirt, completing all four of his passing attempts for 86 yards and two touchdowns while rushing for 51 yards and one touchdown.\nSellers was named the starting quarterback to begin the 2024 season over Auburn transfer Robby Ashford. In his first career start against Old Dominion, he completed 10 of 23 passes for 114 yards while adding 68 rushing yards and a touchdown, including a go-ahead rushing touchdown in the fourth quarter to secure a 23–19 victory. During the season, he led the Gamecocks to a 9–3 record and a No. 15 ranking, highlighted by ranked victories over Texas A&M, Missouri, and Clemson. Against Missouri, Sellers threw for a season-high 353 yards and five touchdowns, including the game-winning 15-yard touchdown pass to Raheim Sanders with 15 seconds remaining. Against Clemson, he scored the go-ahead 20-yard rushing touchdown with less than two minutes remaining to secure a 17–14 Palmetto Bowl victory. In the Citrus Bowl against Illinois, he completed 24 of 34 passes for 260 yards and one touchdown in the loss. Sellers appeared in 12 games and made 12 starts, missing one game due to injury. He completed 196 of 299 passes for 2,534 yards, 18 touchdowns, and seven interceptions while rushing for 674 yards and seven touchdowns. For his performance, he was named the SEC Freshman of the Year, earned third-team All-SEC honors, was selected to the SEC All-Freshman Team, and was recognized as a freshman All-American.\nSellers returned as the starting quarterback for the 2025 season. After leading the Gamecocks to non-conference victories over Virginia Tech and South Carolina State, South Carolina reached a No. 10 ranking before losing seven of its eight conference games and splitting its final two non-conference games. The Gamecocks finished the season with a 4–8 record. Sellers appeared in and started all 12 games, completing 178 of 293 passes for 2,437 yards, 13 touchdowns, and eight interceptions while rushing for 270 yards and five touchdowns."}],"family":[{"relation":"Sibling","name":"Jayden Sellers","description":"American football player (born 2007)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayden_Sellers"}]}}